# Codebase maintenance

Every change should leave the project easier to work in, not harder.

## Scope and focus

- Change only what the task requires; no drive-by refactors or unrelated file edits.
- Match existing naming, folder layout, imports (`#/…` aliases), and component patterns.
- One concern per module — extract helpers or hooks when a file grows unwieldy.

## Quality bar

- Remove unused imports, dead code, and commented-out blocks you introduced.
- Prefer clear names and small functions over clever one-liners.
- Reuse existing utilities and UI primitives (`src/components/ui/`) before adding new ones.
- Keep types accurate; avoid `any` unless the surrounding code already does and you are unblocking a fix.

## Consistency

- Follow the same error-handling and loading patterns as neighboring routes/components.
- Colocate feature code (e.g. `src/components/messaging/`, `src/server-actions/messaging/`).
- Do not add markdown docs or README sections unless the user asks.

## Before finishing

- Mentally lint the touched files: formatting, imports, and obvious type issues.
- If a migration or server function was added, ensure the client and server stay in sync.
